---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ArrowIcon from "../../components/ArrowIcon.astro";
import Disclosure from "../../components/Disclosure.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Local transformations — Mourne & Main" description="Browse clear, respectful before-and-after website concepts for businesses around Dundrum and Newcastle.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="shell page-hero-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Local transformations</p>
        <h1>Judge the work by the difference.</h1>
      </div>
      <p class="page-hero-meta">Each concept starts with public information. Current presentation, proposed change and supporting sources stay visibly separate.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="transformation-list">
    <div class="shell">
      <Disclosure />
      <article class="transformation-card">
        <img src="/images/bucks-head-concept.jpg" alt="Homepage concept for The Bucks Head" width="1265" height="710" />
        <div>
          <span class="tag">Website · Dundrum</span>
          <h2>The Bucks Head</h2>
          <p>The village pub under chef Alex Greene, given a first screen that books tables — date, party and area passing straight into the ResDiary engine it already runs.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/transformations/bucks-head/">Open the comparison <ArrowIcon /></a>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="transformation-card">
        <img src="/images/donard-veterinary-concept.jpg" alt="Homepage concept for Donard Veterinary Clinic" width="1265" height="710" />
        <div>
          <span class="tag">Website · Newcastle</span>
          <h2>Donard Veterinary Clinic</h2>
          <p>The practice's own badge — Mourne silhouette, plum and teal — sets the whole screen, with an appointment-request card up front and the emergency call one tap away.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/transformations/donard-veterinary/">Open the comparison <ArrowIcon /></a>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="transformation-card">
        <img src="/images/mourne-cycles-concept.jpg" alt="Homepage concept for Mourne Cycles" width="1265" height="710" />
        <div>
          <span class="tag">Website · Newcastle</span>
          <h2>Mourne Cycles</h2>
          <p>The area's Trek dealer given back its own name — a storefront opening screen with the range, a bookable workshop and the Cycle to Work saving up front.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/transformations/mourne-cycles/">Open the comparison <ArrowIcon /></a>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="transformation-card">
        <img src="/images/hotel-enniskeen-concept.jpg" alt="Homepage concept for Enniskeen Country House Hotel" width="1265" height="710" />
        <div>
          <span class="tag">Website · Newcastle</span>
          <h2>Enniskeen Country House Hotel</h2>
          <p>A loved, family-run country house reframed around its valley view — with a direct availability path into the hotel's existing booking engine.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/transformations/hotel-enniskeen/">Open the comparison <ArrowIcon /></a>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="transformation-card">
        <img src="/images/castle-farm-concept.png" alt="Homepage concept for Castle Farm Fresh Produce" width="1265" height="710" />
        <div>
          <span class="tag">Website · Dundrum</span>
          <h2>Castle Farm Fresh Produce</h2>
          <p>A calmer arrival, a clear shop action and a stronger explanation of the local product — presented as a direct before-and-after.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/transformations/castle-farm/">Open the comparison <ArrowIcon /></a>
        </div>
      </article>
      <div class="coming-row" aria-label="Next research subjects">
        <article class="coming-card"><span>Concept queue · Both towns</span><h3>Five verified prospects</h3><p>From Dundrum caf&eacute;s to a hardware yard and a seaside amusement arcade — researched and verified against public sources in July 2026.</p></article>
        <article class="coming-card"><span>Community queue · Newcastle</span><h3>Newcastle Chamber of Commerce</h3><p>A civic hub concept planned as a visible community contribution.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
